<p>British Prime Minister Keir Starmer said he would remain in office after Labour suffered heavy losses in elections across England, Scotland and Wales, prompting calls from some Labour MPs for him to resign. The votes covered English local councils and the devolved parliaments in Scotland and Wales, making them the largest electoral test of Starmer&#x27;s government since Labour&#x27;s 2024 general-election victory. Reform UK, led by Nigel Farage, made large gains in English councils. Dawn reported that the party had gained more than 700 council seats in England while results were still being counted. Labour also lost power in Wales, where Plaid Cymru won 43 of the 96 Senedd seats, Reform UK won 34 and Labour fell to nine; Welsh Labour leader and First Minister Eluned Morgan lost her seat and said she would step down as party leader. In Scotland, the SNP won the Holyrood election but fell short of an overall majority, while Labour and Reform UK tied for second with 17 seats each.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Xb4ZiUWFgMseemvdAHCKdKkZAb0JfyAfIcmuI15Lg_4S7-ZGyvvXVH5_zNOMvJQYeuODCLmxedy8182rPvT_rRQpbTlRcemP7j5Itvbo-QXzAY63okz3w0OPHI1iwf8PVG_rMx4ORVDXc0BVQirhB9f19u1d0PHVayUjkfhL03kOr1GdUuVj5fw1WW2I2jjUN_XWmxbgC-9qQMvNqgclQ27ma6fJGLH4yzkbx4Y8fihsPVViJBSmqd0086tvu7zFAk4PYIc208FOUeteEQ' alt='British Prime Minister and Labour leader Keir Starmer speaks to supporters at Kingsdown Methodist Church in London on Friday after local election losses.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Leadership pressure: A Guardian poll found 45% of Labour members surveyed said Starmer should step down, while 42% named Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham as their first choice to succeed him.</li><li>Left competition: The Green Party made gains in progressive urban areas and won its first mayoral victory, while the Liberal Democrats also claimed wins in the election round.</li><li>Heartland losses: Reform won all 14 seats Labour defended in Tameside and all 20 contested Labour-held seats in Wigan, according to reports on early English council results.</li><li>Scottish Greens: The Scottish Greens won their first Holyrood constituency seats and recorded their best Scottish Parliament result, adding pressure on both the SNP and Labour in Scotland.</li></ul><blockquote>I am not going to walk away - Keir Starmer</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Keir Starmer: Starmer said Labour had to give voters a clearer sense of hope and spell out the steps his government would take after the midterm defeats. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/uk-election-mauling-leaves-keir-starmer-promising-hope-but-little-change/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Nigel Farage: Farage said the results showed &quot;an historic shift in British politics&quot; and told reporters, &quot;I think the best is yet to come,&quot; while arguing Reform UK could translate local gains into national power. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/nigel-farage-reform-uk-win-next-general-election/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>John Swinney: Swinney challenged Starmer to show &quot;greater respect&quot; to Scotland&#x27;s government after the SNP secured another Holyrood victory. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/may/08/john-swinney-declares-victory-for-snp-in-holyrood-elections'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Rhun ap Iorwerth: Plaid Cymru&#x27;s leader said he was ready to become first minister and form the next Welsh government after his party topped the Senedd vote. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/may/08/plaid-cymru-biggest-party-wales-senedd-labour-reform'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>John Curtice: Curtice said Labour&#x27;s showing was &quot;pretty much as bad as anyone expected for Labour, or worse,&quot; after early results showed losses in traditional strongholds. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458614/uks-labour-party-suffers-heavy-early-losses-as-reform-gains-in-elections'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https: